In my experience a cat on the way down through mine town might or might
not attack the watchmen.  I've lost pets to watchmen on the way down. 
Especially I've lost pets to the watch captain's sword.  Pets on the way
back up from ines end, on the other hand, tend to be strong enough to
take out the watchmen and watch captain easily.  On the way back up the
problem tends to be closing doors to keep shopkeepers or priests alive.

The watch has okay armor.  Often enough one will have a studded leather
armor.  Until dragon scales it's the best body armor that does not
interfere with spell casting.  For a spell casting charter it is a hard
trade off between the betterAC of mithril and the zero spell
interference of studded leather.

>> Keep sticking with darts and daggers? Worth
>> skilling up any other melee weapons?
>
> Lacking an appropriate artifact weapon I enjoy switching to a crysknife.

Daggers can be multifired, knives can not.  Even those healer maxes out
at basic in dagger that's still a 50-50 chance of firing 1-vs-2 daggers
from your quiver every time.  At very least use daggers enough to
enhance them to skilled then gather a dozen or so for your quiver.

It takes a while for long worms to get spawned in the dungeon.  It's
easy to reach the mine town alter and get an artifact gift before that
happens in dungeons that have a co-aligned priest.  In dungeons that
have a cross-aligned priest it's not unusual to encounter a long worm on
the way back up from mines end but artifact gifts don't need 2+ enchant
weapons scrolls to convert and fix.

And use that altar to max out your luck.  Search out all of the dart
traps in the mines and have a lot of them in a stack ready to use an
early holy water to bless them so the big stack can last you the rest of
the game.


